# <module> - MODULE.md

Template for every `godot/src/<module>/MODULE.md` (03 s15.1, ADR-14, TA-06). Copy it, keep every heading in
this order, delete no heading (write "None." under it if empty). Max 300 lines. Replace the `<...>` placeholders
and the hint lines in italics. Signatures are copied from the code; `tools/gen_module_api.py --check` (TA-27)
fails CI when they disagree.

| Field | Value |
|---|---|
| Responsibility | one paragraph: what this module owns and what it explicitly does not |
| Lane owner tier | Fable / Opus / Sonnet / Haiku for typical tasks (ADR-14) |
| May depend on | list from 01 s9.2 (mirrored in `tools/deps.json`) |
| Must never touch | list |
| Autoloads used | none / Log / ContentDB / App |
| Status | stub / API frozen (date) / implemented / native twin planned |

## Public API

GDScript signatures only, grouped by class. Every public symbol here is covered by a test listed below.
Anything not listed is private even if GDScript cannot enforce it (prefix `_`).

```gdscript
class_name <Name> extends <Base>     # one line of purpose; autoloads have no class_name (CLAUDE.md)
static func <name>(<arg>: <Type>) -> <Type>
```

`gen_module_api.py --check` compares every top-level `class_name` (+ `extends`), `func`/`static func`, `signal`, `const`, `var`
and `enum` here with the code (`_private` names skipped). Consts, vars and enums may be grouped or listed as ranges, but a listed
one must exist; every public `func`/`signal` in the code must be listed. Several statements per line with `;` are fine.
Planned-but-unwritten API is marked so the check passes until the code lands: `# [planned]`, `# [planned: TA-12]` or
`# [owner-task: TA-12]` in the comment of a line marks that line; on a `class_name` line it marks the class (it may be absent
and its missing members are tolerated); or put one `# planned: ClassA, ClassB` comment line first in the block. Delete the
marker when the task lands (symbols that exist are compared regardless). Autoloads: a bare `Log` line or
`# autoload: godot/src/<module>/<file>.gd` before their members.

## Invariants

Numbered, testable statements ("I3: `height_at` returns identical values for identical inputs on server and client").
A change to this section or to Public API is a contract change: the contract tests change first, in the same PR (ADR-11).

## Data owned

Packed arrays, side tables, files on disk, JSON defs read. *Hint: name the owner of each piece of state.*

## Events emitted / consumed

`SimEvent` kinds, signals (presentation only), commands accepted. *Hint: write None. for pure modules.*

## Performance budget

Per tick or per frame, from 03 s4.2 / s10.2, with the perf scenario that measures it.

## Test entry points

Existing paths under `godot/test/` or `tools/tests/` go in backticks: check_deps D10 verifies that every backticked
path here exists. Planned tests go in plain text (no backticks) until the file is on disk.

